//! block-shape.rs's walkBlocks/flattenBlocks and atlas-test-map.rs's coveredPaths). `T`,
//! `BANK_TAGS`, `BANK_COUNT` ARE ported below as pressed `LazyLock<Value>` statics (class 'const',
//! same convention as rt-emotion.rs/rt-play.rs) — hand-appended, not expand.mjs-generated, because
//! this file mixes consts with real functions (fill/rng/makePicker) and the generator refuses
//! mixed files. Values pressed directly from the live JS module (T = {...CORE, ...EMOTION,
//! ...PLAY}); CORE itself (the ~1050-line inline template-array literal) has no separate Rust
//! identifier since it is not exported by the JS — it only exists merged into T.
